<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maharashtra</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maharashtra is a state of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, created in 1960 from the Marathi-speaking parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bombay-state">Bombay State</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mumbai">Mumbai</a> as its capital. Its territory includes the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konkan-coast">Konkan coast</a> and much of the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan-plateau">Deccan plateau</a>. The region was ruled in turn by the Satavahanas, Rashtrakutas, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seuna-yadava-dynasty">Yadavas of Devagiri</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan-sultanates">Deccan sultanates</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a>, and it is the heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marathi">Marathi</a> language.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maharashtra.jpg" alt="Maharashtra" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jawahar Soneji · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gateway_of_India_-Mumbai.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
